From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:23:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: drop the camera provider 2.4 HAL for now

camera.sdm710.so segfaults during get_number_of_cameras(): CamX fails to
probe sensor 1 (CSLHwInternalProbeSensorHW() ioctl on /dev/v4l-subdev7
returns ENODEV, the kernel logs cam_cci_read read_words = 0), then
ImageSensorUtils::GetTunedColorCorrectionData() calls GetChromatix() on
the null TuningDataManager that leaves behind.

That is not a camera bug on its own -- it is a boot bug. init counts the
5th crash before sys.boot_completed, sets sys.init.updatable_crashing,
and apexd responds with "Native process 'vendor.camera-provider-2-4' is
crashing. Attempting a revert" and reboots. The device never finishes a
boot, and the reason is invisible unless the HAL's tombstone is read.

Stop packaging the provider, its passthrough impl and camera.device@3.2,
and drop the matching VINTF entry. The sensor probe is its own gap.

---
 device.mk    | 14 ++++++++++----
 manifest.xml |  9 ---------
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index 20b7be38..b4e8e77a 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -413,10 +413,16 @@ PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
     debug.media.transcoding.codec_max_operating_rate_1080P=120 \
     debug.media.transcoding.codec_max_operating_rate_4K=50 \
 
-PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
-    android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4-impl \
-    android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4-service_64 \
-    camera.device@3.2-impl
+# lineage-24.0: the CamX stack cannot probe sensor 1 on this kernel
+# (CSLHwInternalProbeSensorHW ioctl -> ENODEV on /dev/v4l-subdev7, cam_cci_read returns 0 words),
+# so camera.sdm710.so leaves the sensor's TuningDataManager null and GetChromatix() segfaults in
+# get_number_of_cameras(). init then counts 5 crashes before boot_completed, sets
+# sys.init.updatable_crashing, and apexd reverts and reboots -- the HAL takes the whole boot with
+# it. Do not ship it until the sensor probe is fixed; nothing else needs it to boot.
+#PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+#    android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4-impl \
+#    android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4-service_64 \
+#    camera.device@3.2-impl
 
 PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
     $(LOCAL_PATH)/sensors/hals.conf:vendor/etc/sensors/hals.conf
diff --git a/manifest.xml b/manifest.xml
index 76e3d853..038010d4 100644
--- a/manifest.xml
+++ b/manifest.xml
@@ -35,15 +35,6 @@
             <instance>default</instance>
         </interface>
     </hal>
-    <hal format="hidl">
-        <name>android.hardware.camera.provider</name>
-        <transport>hwbinder</transport>
-        <version>2.4</version>
-        <interface>
-            <name>ICameraProvider</name>
-            <instance>legacy/0</instance>
-        </interface>
-    </hal>
     <hal format="hidl">
         <name>android.hardware.gatekeeper</name>
         <transport>hwbinder</transport>
